Z||000000||redfiero||08-16-2000||06:58 AM||||Anyone know what the sequence and tightening specs. are for an 88 Chevy 305?  I'm removing them to have the valves done this weekend.<P>Thanks,<BR>matt||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||08-16-2000||02:19 PM||||Yes, start from the inner most bolt and work outward in a circle. Picture in your mind that there is a bubble in the center if the head and your job is to squeeze that bubble out. You wouldn't squeeze a tube of toothpaste in the middle to get the last drop out... would you? The best thing to do if you're not too sure is go to the local library and look at their reference books. All SMC, up to the LT1, have the same sequence. Not sure about the torque but I would guess around 75 ft/lbs.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||08-17-2000||12:34 PM||||When I get home tonight, I'll post a diagram and the torque specs for the small block Chevys heads.||||reg||1
